Language English
Debug Off

Book Endings
	Triggered By @GameOver
	
	Page HardFail Like UIOpeningText
		Visible When firstRitual

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			The house shakes, and light streams up through the floorboards and,
			somehow, through the cave walls. With a thunderous clap and a shock
			wave of power, the ceiling rains down as the house begins to
			collapse. You run toward the servant dining room, but when you get
			there, cult members block your path. They attack you without mercy.
			
			As you lie on the floor, bleeding and dying, the cultists run out
			the door to safety. Sarah leans down and whispers, <<We failed and
			there is no telling how much of the world will be destroyed, how
			many people will die. But you did your best, so thank you.>>

			Your last living experience is the floor under you rising up as the
			Ancient One enters the world.
			
			The end.
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "HardFail.English.ogg"
	End Page HardFail

	Page OpenGateWin Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalOpenGate And outcome = gameWin

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			You run out the door of the Chapel, breathing hard and nearly
			carrying the boy with you. Sarah follows you outside into the night.
			The full moon shines down, showing the path is clear of cultists.
			You are finally safe.

			Sarah turns to you and says, <<You were successful. Not only did we
			stop Matthias's current plans, we stopped anyone's ability to use
			this area to try again. Our nephew will grow up normally and I can
			finally find peace. Thank you.>>

			As you walk down the road, you reflect
			on everything that just happened. Exhausted and still in shock, you
			wonder if the world will ever feel the same again. But you are also
			deeply comforted and proud that you were able to save the world from
			the evil that Matthias tried to bring.

			The end.
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "OpenGateWin.English.ogg"
	End Page OpenGateWin
	
	Page OpenGateDraw Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalOpenGate And outcome = gameDraw

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			You run out the door of the Chapel, breathing hard, still panicked.
			Sarah follows you outside into the night. The full moon shines down,
			showing the path is clear of cultists. You are finally safe.

			Sarah turns to you and says, <<You were successful. But you were not
			able to seal the gate, so this will all happen again. I need to get
			back to our nephew, to see if there is anything I can do for him.
			Once he dies, I will try to send him to find peace. I will stay and
			wait for the next opportunity to permanently stop this madness.
			Thank you for what you were able to do.>>

			As you walk down the road, you reflect on everything that happened.
			Exhausted and still in shock, you wonder if the world will ever feel
			the same again. While knowing you stopped his plans, Matthias still
			brutally killed his son. But you are at least comforted that you
			were able to save the world from the evil that Matthias tried to
			bring.

			The end.
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "OpenGateDraw.English.ogg"
	End Page OpenGateDraw
	
	Page OpenGateLose Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalOpenGate And outcome = gameLose

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			As the Ancient One's tentacle comes farther through the  portal, the altar room shakes and stone
			from the ceiling starts to fall. Your cousin smiles... his work is done.

			You find a door that leads back to the cave, but when you enter, you
			find yourself surrounded by more cultists. This time, they outnumber
			you. You fall quickly to their weapons.

			Broken and bleeding, you lie on the floor. A monstrous roar cuts
			through the din:  the Ancient One has come through the gate. As you
			draw your last breath, the cultists fall to their knees and begin
			praying to their god for salvation.
			
			The only comfort you have is in knowing that a stream of sacrifice
			is required to keep the Ancient One here. With so many cult members
			dead, maybe It won't be here for long.
			
			The last thing you feel is the ceiling caving in and the screams of
			the cultists, betrayed by their god for their foolishness. 

			
			The end.
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "OpenGateLose.English.ogg"
	End Page OpenGateLose
	
	Page FeedGateWin Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalFeedGate And outcome = gameWin

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			As the last cultist falls---and with Matthias dead---the gate begins
			to sputter. When you complete the sealing spell, the gate collapses
			and the boy falls to the ground with a thud. He burns like coals, his
			eyes open wide in terror and pain. He moves his mouth but no sound
			comes out.

			Sarah turns to you and says, <<You were successful. Not only did we
			stop Matthias's plans, we stopped anyone's ability to use this area
			to try again. I only wish our nephew were able to survive, but I 
			don't think there was a way. I will stay with him here, then help him
			find peace once he dies. Thank you.>>

			As you exit the chapel into the moonlit night, you reflect on what
			happened these last hours: the mystery, the fear, and the death. And
			your nephew. Thinking of him smoldering back there makes your gorge
			rise. You wonder if the world will ever feel the same. But you
			are also deeply comforted and proud that you were able to save the
			world from the evil that Matthias tried to bring.
			
			The end.
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "FeedGateWin.English.ogg"
	End Page FeedGateWin
	
	Page FeedGateDraw Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalFeedGate And outcome = gameDraw

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame

		Text """
			The last cultist falls at your feet. You stagger back, broken and
			bleeding. Unable to stand, you fall to the floor. Without Matthias to keep it open and
			the cultists to offer sacrifice, the gate begins to sputter. A
			tentacle tentatively pokes through, but pulls back when the gate
			suddenly pops.

			Sarah leans down and whispers, <<"The Ancient One will not make it
			through. But you were not able to seal the gate, so it can
			happen here again. When the gate collapses, our nephew will die. I will
			see him to peace. Then I will return and wait for the next attempt.>>

			The last thing you see is Sarah softly calling your nephew's name
			while the gate destabilizes. As you die you are at least a little
			comforted by what you were able to accomplish. You saved the world.
			For now at least. 

			The End.
		"""

		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "FeedGateDraw.English.ogg"
	End Page FeedGateDraw
	
	Page FeedGateLose Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalFeedGate And outcome = gameLose

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			The cultists beat and stab you to the ground and eventually you are
			unable to fight back. One-by-one, you watch cultists
			approach the gate, draw daggers, and slit their own throats.
			As another draws across his neck, tentacles begin coming through the
			gate. The room is shaking and the ceiling starts to fall. 

			Sarah leans in and whispers, <<We failed. The Ancient One is here.
			With your unused elder sign, someone else could fix the gate to keep
			it open. Our nephew could remain as the gate indefinitely, a fate
			much worse than death. I will stay and try to find a way to close
			the gate, but the world is in trouble.>>

			The last thing you hear before it all goes dark is Sarah. <<Thank
			you for trying. You did the best that you could.>>

			The end.		
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "FeedGateLose.English.ogg"
	End Page FeedGateLose
	
	Page CloseGateWin Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalCloseGate And outcome = gameWin

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			The gate winks out and the boy falls to the ground, smoldering like
			coals in a fire pit. The elder sign is embedded in his forehead,
			unnoticed in the pain of the fire.

			Sarah leans in and whispers, <<You were successful in stopping
			Matthias and his plans to remake the world. You also stopped anyone
			else from trying it here again. Once the boy dies, I will help him
			find peace, then I will be able to rest. Thank you.>>

			As you exit the chapel into the moonlit night, you reflect on what
			happened these last hours. The mystery, the fear, and the death.
			And your nephew. Thinking of him burning back there makes your gorge
			rise.

			Exhausted and still in shock, you wonder if the world will ever feel
			the same again. But you are also deeply comforted and proud that you
			were able to save the world from the evil that Matthias tried to
			bring.

			The end.		
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "CloseGateWin.English.ogg"
	End Page CloseGateWin
	
	Page CloseGateDraw Like UIOpeningText
		Visible If goal = goalCloseGate And outcome = gameDraw

		Trigger @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Text """
			When you complete the closing spell, the cave shakes, the gate
			flashes and pops twice, then winks out of existence. The boy falls to the
			floor with a thud. He is smoldering like hot coals; his eyes are wide with fear and pain; his mouth
			moves but no sound comes out. 

			Sarah turns to you and says, <<You were successful. But you were not
			able to seal the gate, so this will all happen again. Once the boy
			dies, I will try to send him to find peace. I will stay and
			wait for the next opportunity to permanently stop this madness. 
			Thank you for what you were able to do.>>

			As you exit the chapel into the moonlit night, you reflect on what
			happened these last hours. The mystery, the fear, and the death. And
			your nephew. Thinking of him burning back there makes your gorge
			rise.

			But at least the world is safe tonight. 

			The end.		
		"""
		
		Add UIEndButton
		Audio "CloseGateDraw.English.ogg"
	End Page CloseGateDraw
	
	Page CloseGateLose
		Visible If goal = goalCloseGate And outcome = gameLose
		No Text
		
		Goto OpenGateLose
	End Page CloseGateLose
	
	Page ShowUIFrame
		Triggered By @ShowIntroFrame
		
		Add UIStoryImage, UIStoryBackground, UIOpeningText, UISplashFancyBar 
		No Text
	End Page ShowUIFrame
	
	Page HideIntroFrame
		Triggered By @HideIntroFrame
		Remove UIStoryImage, UIStoryBackground, UISplashFancyBar, UIStoryContinue, UIEndGame
		No Text
	End Page HideIntroFrame
End Book Endings

